# cylinder_bore_rough.cam — flank roughing fixture (DECISIONS.md "stock_to_leave
# first slice…"). The cylinder_bore.cam bore wall run as a ROUGHING pass with a
# 0.5mm allowance. A flank's stepdown is purely axial, so it leaves NO cusp:
# the cusp budget is exactly 0.000mm and the whole allowance becomes radial
# skin. Engine mode's tool-centre ring shrinks to 20 − 5 − 0.5 = 14.5mm
# (X64.5, the hand-checked anchor); control mode emits the ROUGHED wall
# (19.5mm, X69.5) as its part edge while the D register stays the pure tool
# radius — the allowance is engine-baked in both comp modes, so a double-comp
# is unrepresentable. The wall is still cut to FULL depth: the radial skin is
# the wall's, and a floor's skin belongs to a floor op.
units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000

stock Box(w=100, l=100, h=20, x=0, y=0, z=0)

tool T5 Endmill(dia=10.0)

feature Bore CylinderBore(dia=40.0, extent=12.0, x=50.0, y=50.0)

run Side(tool=T5, surface=Bore, stepover=5.0, stock_to_leave=0.5)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=Bore, stepover=5.0, comp=control, stock_to_leave=0.5)
